From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:04:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] x86: SMSW r16 keeps its operand-size prefix

NASM 3.02 folded the memory and 16-bit register forms of SMSW into one
template, in x86/insns.dat:

    SMSW	rm16	[m:	0f 01 /4]	286

with no operand-size prefix. A 16-bit register matches it before the
sized templates below it, so in 32-bit and 64-bit code `smsw bx`
assembles to 0F 01 E3, which is `smsw ebx` and stores all of EBX.
NASM 2.16.03 assembled 66 0F 01 E3, the 16-bit form the SDM defines,
which leaves the register's upper half alone.

FEX-2610's 32-bit Secondary/07_XX_04 test depends on that: it loads
0x41424344 into EBX, runs `smsw bx` and expects 0x41420033. Assembled
by 3.02 it ends with EBX 0x80050033 on the gadget engine and on the
x86-64 JIT alike; the 2.16.03 binary passes on both. Limit the template
to a word memory operand and let a register operand select the sized
templates below it, which restores the 2.16.03 encoding in 16-bit,
32-bit and 64-bit code.
---
 x86/insns.dat | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/x86/insns.dat b/x86/insns.dat
index a5961669be1417b10af51a4d1d67de2d4eb10cc5..d87211508ab7380adbcc565778279158aea55dac 100644
--- a/x86/insns.dat
+++ b/x86/insns.dat
@@ -439,7 +439,7 @@ $dq   RDPID	reg#				[m:	f3 !osp o# 0f c7 /7]			RDPID
       CLTS	void				[	0f 06]					286,PRIV
       CPUID	void				[	0f a2]					PENT
       LMSW	rm16				[m:	0f 01 /6]				286,PRIV
-      SMSW	rm16				[m:	0f 01 /4]				286
+      SMSW	mem16				[m:	0f 01 /4]				286
       SMSW	reg64				[m:	o64nw 0f 01 /4]				X86_64,LONG,ND
 $wdq  SMSW	reg#				[m:	o# 0f 01 /4]				286
 
